export const README_TEXT = `These are your books.

This folder was created by Accnomos. Everything the app knows about your business is in here, in plain files:
- 00 Inbox: drop receipts, invoices or statements here (photo, PDF, email attachment) and Accnomos will read them.
- 01 Receipts: purchase documents Accnomos has filed, by month, renamed like "2026-10-21 Screwfix £38.47.pdf".
- 02 Needs a look: anything odd (duplicates, missing VAT number, unreadable), with a reason. Nothing in here is posted.
- 03 Sales: sales documents. Invoices you write in Accnomos are in invoices/, and the exact PDF each customer was sent is in invoices/sent/.
- 04 Bank statements: the bank statement files you imported.
- 05 Payroll: pay run exports for your payroll provider, one per month.
- 06 VAT returns: the 9-box calculation and HMRC receipt for each period.
- 07 Reports: reports you asked Accnomos to save.
- Books.xlsx: a spreadsheet of your books, rebuilt from the files in _System. Do not edit it; it is overwritten.
- Archive, Backups, Accnomos Backups, _Trash: made when first used. Archive holds older years you archived
  (same subfolders), Backups dated copies of _System, Accnomos Backups the full backups you made with
  "Back up now" (one dated folder each, with RESTORE.txt inside), and _Trash anything the app would otherwise
  delete (duplicates, old backups). Accnomos never empties _Trash; you can, in OneDrive.
- _System: the ledger events and the audit log (never edited: a correction is a new entry that reverses
  the old one), plus rules you approved, contacts, jobs, staff, timesheets, vehicles and your mileage log.

You can open all of this without the app. If you disconnect Accnomos, the files stay yours.
Sample data is labelled "SAMPLE — FICTIONAL COMPANY".
`;
